# Reference Wrapped v33

Unapproved shading concept. Built-in image generation. User correction: planar horizontal cloud flow must wrap circumferentially, including shadow silhouettes; vertical axis becomes radial, crown inward/base outward. Final image removes screen-horizontal inward tongues. Reference silhouette fidelity and excess small interior details remain review items. No level replacement or packed opacity data.

## Initial prompt

Create a corrected square polar UV cloud atlas. Image 1 is the user's directional correction diagram: orange path indicates CONTINUOUS LONGITUDINAL CLOUD FLOW around circumference, NOT a decoration to reproduce. Image 2 is original planar cloud STYLE AND SHAPE reference.
KEY CORRECTION: Treat the original horizontal panorama cloud bank as ONE LONG CONNECTED STRIP and BEND its horizontal axis around the orange circular path, like wrapping a panorama onto an annulus. All long cloud shelves, longitudinal shadow shapes and elongated cloud bodies must RUN TANGENTIALLY ALONG THE CIRCLE, continuously from top-right down right side, across bottom and up left side. Do not rotate and stamp individual vertical cloud modules. Do not build a radial flower made of round isolated blobs or fingers. The original panorama's vertical axis becomes radial: cloud tops toward center, bottoms toward exterior. The original panorama's horizontal axis becomes circumferential. Every originally horizontal shadow shelf bends along the SAME ARC. At right the cloud bank and shadow shelves run vertically along circle; at bottom they run horizontally; at left they run vertically. NOT straight horizontal brush streaks across atlas.
Compose an asymmetrical broad connected right-to-bottom cloud belt tapering into much thinner connected distant cloud shelves up left. Leave broad empty center and a modest natural opening near 11 o'clock. Preserve original reference's wide low cloud formations, several broad irregular tall rises on right, relatively low left distant banks. The cloud is a continuous landscape bank wrapped around circle, not evenly repeated scallops. Rounded gently varied inward silhouette, large flat connected light-gray crown planes, broad darker-gray underside planes nearer outer circumference. Reference's shadow silhouettes are long, quiet, irregular connected shapes flowing along bank. Restrained animation background paint, very little small detail. No big separate circular gray cells. Outer underside slightly softened, readable broad outline, no geometric circle clipping. Opaque pure black empty sky and margin, NO transparency/checkerboard, no colored arrows, no text, logos, scene objects. Grayscale shading artwork only.

## Direction correction

Correct the image's geometric orientation. The long thin horizontal shelves jutting into black center are WRONG. REMOVE ALL of them and replace with smooth broad connected cloud masses that follow the circular arc. Right-side clouds must be SIDEWAYS: their growth/up direction is LEFT, their base/down direction is RIGHT. They must NOT look like upright clouds stacked vertically. Rotate their internal shading too so long shadow bases on right run VERTICALLY, curving with perimeter. On left cloud up direction is RIGHT and base is LEFT. On bottom up is UP. At upper right up is DOWN-LEFT. Maintain grayscale broad painted planes, asymmetrical thick right belt and thin left belt, wide black center. Make ONE continuous cloud bank whose longitudinal axis bends all around circumference. No horizontal tongues, no flat shelves jutting into center, no repeated upright islands. Inner edge should be rounded bulges connected by shallow valleys, outer edge dark gently softened base. Long shadows follow the arc tangentially. No radial spokes. Keep pure black background and no annotations.
